A||N||0||Will||Had a good run with a..... Geo??||||1||
Z||000000||Will||01-09-2001||11:11 AM||||I was on my two hour (only on weekends) commute home from work, which involves crossing a mountain. At the base of the mountain I was behind a Geo Metro who was behind a van. When the road opened up the Geo and I both passed the van. The Geo then proceded to surprise the hell out of me by hustling up the mountain, going just a tick slower than I would under similar ciculmstances. That side of the mountain is very tight with few straight stretches, so I stayed behind him because the road was damp and the center lane was full of sand and salt. There is a fairly straight stretch near the top where I was able to get around him. The other side of the mountain is not quite as tight with a few more straight stretches. I pushed it pretty hard through the corners, just about drifting a pretty tight hairpin. I was pulling away in the corners, but I let off in the straights to let him catch up. He was hardly glued to my bumper, but he was keeping up. When we got off the mountain and the road opened up into divided highway I slowed down to let him pass me. I gave him the thumbs up as he went by and he waved.<P>To date the fastest cars I have seen on twisty roads have been that Geo and an 80's Escort. (If anyone goes to Virginia Tech I had a little fun with the Escort on the Ironto road. Aside from me that was the fastest driver I've ever seen on that road)<P>Anyway, it was a lot of fun and a nice test of skill.||||reg||1
